# Unit Testing (Phase 2)

> **When to apply:** After Phase 1 implementation is complete. See `00-workflow/000-rules-sequence.mdc`.

## Scope

| Target | Requirement |
|--------|-------------|
| `src/lib/**` utils | Unit test every new or changed util |
| `src/hooks/**` and feature/module hooks | Unit test pure logic; mock React Query / router where needed |
| `src/components/ui/**` | Component test with React Testing Library — render + a11y queries, not snapshot-only |
| Zod schemas (`schemas/`, `schema.ts`) | At least one valid + one invalid case per schema |

## Conventions

- **Runner:** Vitest
- **Location:** all tests live under `tests/` at the repo root — **never** in `src/`
- **Mirror `src/` paths:** `src/features/orders/hooks/useOrders.ts` → `tests/features/orders/hooks/useOrders.test.ts`
- **Shared helpers:** `tests/helpers/` (import via `@tests/helpers/...`)
- **Import production code** via `@/` only — no relative imports into `src/`
- **Naming:** `describe('<UnitName>', () => { it('should ...', () => {}) })`
- **No `test.skip` or `test.only`** merged to main
- **Coverage gate:** ≥ 70% lines on `src/lib` and `src/hooks` (CI target)

## What to test

```ts
// ✅ util — pure function
describe('formatFileSize', () => {
  it('should format megabytes correctly', () => {
    expect(formatFileSize(1024 * 1024)).toBe('1.00 MB');
  });
});

// ✅ schema — valid + invalid
describe('createAPIKeySchema', () => {
  it('accepts valid input', () => { /* ... */ });
  it('rejects empty name', () => { /* ... */ });
});

// ✅ component — behavior, not snapshots
describe('NameField', () => {
  it('shows validation error when name is empty', () => { /* RTL + userEvent */ });
});
```

## Commands

```bash
yarn vitest run                              # all tests once
yarn vitest run tests/path/to/Foo.test.ts    # single file
yarn vitest run tests/shared/modules/**      # module tests
```

## Do not

- Write tests before implementation (Phase 1) unless the prompt is test-only
- Use snapshot-only tests as the sole coverage for a component
- Mock everything — prefer testing real util logic and shallow component behavior
